# How to Start

Follow these steps to set up and run the project locally.

## Prerequisites

- Node.js (v18 or higher recommended)
- MySQL (running locally or hosted)

## Setup Steps

### 1. Clone the Repository & Install Dependencies

```bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd <repo-name>
npm install
```

### 2. Configure Environment Variables

Copy `.env.example` to a new file named `.env`:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Open `.env` and fill in your actual database credentials.

### 3. Initialize the Database

```bash
node config/initDb.js
```

### 4. Start the Application

```bash
npm start
```

The application will run at:

```
http://localhost:3000
```

(or your configured port).

---

# Project Flow (How the Code Works)

This project uses the **Model-View-Controller (MVC)** architectural pattern. The following diagram illustrates how a request travels through the application.

```text
               ┌────────────────────────┐
               │    Client/Browser      │ <────────────────────────┐
               └────────────────────────┘                          │
                           │ (HTTP Request)                        │
                           ▼                                       │ (HTML Rendered)
                     ┌───────────┐                                 │
                     │  app.js   │ (Entry Point)                   │
                     └───────────┘                                 │
                           │                                       │
                           ▼                                       │
                   ┌──────────────┐                                │
                   │   routes/    │                                │
                   └──────────────┘                                │
                           │                                       │
                           ▼                                       │
                ┌──────────────────┐                               │
                │   middleware/    │ (e.g., Session check)         │
                └──────────────────┘                               │
                           │                                       │
                           ▼                                       │
                ┌──────────────────┐                               │
                │   controllers/   │ ──────────────────────────────┘
                └──────────────────┘
                     │        │
         (Fetch/Save)│        │ (Passes Data)
                     ▼        ▼
               ┌────────┐  ┌────────┐
               │ models/│  │ views/ │ (EJS Templates)
               └────────┘  └────────┘
                   │
                   ▼
               ┌────────┐
               │ config/│ (Database)
               └────────┘
```

## Flow Breakdown

### app.js

Initializes Express, registers global middlewarses, and links to your `routes/`.

### routes/

Matches the incoming URL path (e.g., `/admin/dashboard`) and routes it.

### middleware/

Intercepts requests to check authentication (`authMiddleware.js`) or validate input data (`validators.js`) before letting them proceed.

### controllers/

Handles the main business logic (e.g., `adminController.js` handles loading the dashboard data).

### models/ & config/

The controller talks to your model (`userModel.js`) to query/write data to MySQL (`db.js`).

### views/

The controller renders the correct `.ejs` template, injecting any dynamic data to send back to the user's browser.